commit 669809d5c6110796b36b32fe26073376a605911d
f64::MAX = (2^53-1)*2^971 = 1.7976931348623157e+308; log2 = 1024.00000000000000000

== 1-2. curve orders, n^4 against f64::MAX ==
curve            n_bits order ok    log2(n^4) n^4>MAX exact   f64(n)^4 k_bits 3n/4 table k
secp192k1           192     True   768.000000         False     finite         144     144
secp224k1           225     True   896.000000         False     finite         168     168
secp256k1           256     True  1024.000000          True        inf         192     192
P-256               256     True  1024.000000         False     finite         192     192
brainpoolP256r1     256     True  1021.636946         False     finite         192     192
P-384               384     True  1536.000000          True        inf         288     288
brainpoolP384r1     384     True  1532.546862          True        inf         288     288
P-521               521     True  2084.000000          True        inf         390     384

Claims: only secp256k1 among the 256-bit curves has n^4 > f64::MAX; every 384-bit curve does.
  256-bit curves with n^4 > MAX: ['secp256k1']
  384-bit curves with n^4 > MAX: ['P-384', 'brainpoolP384r1']
  P-521 floor(3*521/4) = 390; probes use 384 = 3/4*512: True
  2^256 - n(secp256k1): log2 = 128.346; 2^256 - n(P-256): log2 = 224.000
  n(secp256k1) - n(P-256): log2 = 224.000   (analysis §10.1 says '~2^192')
  log2(f64::MAX) = 1024.000000   (analysis §10.1 says 'f64::MAX ~ 2^1023')
  P-256 n^4 / f64::MAX = 0.999999999069 (below 1 by ~2^-30.0)

== 3. P-521 scaled diagonal and the first GS subtraction (row m against rows 0..m-1) ==
bits(n^2) = 1042; scale_shift = max_bits - 500 = 542
exact n^2 / 2^542 = 2^500 * (1 - 1.917e-79)
  round-to-nearest (num-bigint 0.5.1 to_f64): diag == 2^500: True; diag = 2^500*(1 - 0.000e+00); max |b*_m[l]| after subtracting mu*b*_l over 64 random a_l: 0.0
  truncation (hypothetical): diag == 2^500: False; diag = 2^500*(1 - 1.110e-16); max |b*_m[l]| after subtracting mu*b*_l over 64 random a_l: 3.6341936214780345e+134 (= 2^447.0)
  true scaled b*_m[m] = 2^384 / 2^542 = 2^-158

== 4. residual-dominates condition: true component 2^k_bits/2^shift below one ulp of the scaled n*a entries ==
  P-256            shift= 12  scaled n*a ~ 2^500  ulp ~ 2^447  true b*_m[m] = 2^180  dominated: True
  brainpoolP256r1  shift= 11  scaled n*a ~ 2^500  ulp ~ 2^447  true b*_m[m] = 2^181  dominated: True
  brainpoolP384r1  shift=267  scaled n*a ~ 2^500  ulp ~ 2^447  true b*_m[m] = 2^21  dominated: True
  P-384            shift=268  scaled n*a ~ 2^500  ulp ~ 2^447  true b*_m[m] = 2^20  dominated: True
  secp256k1        shift= 12  scaled n*a ~ 2^500  ulp ~ 2^447  true b*_m[m] = 2^180  dominated: True
  P-521            shift=542  scaled n*a ~ 2^500  ulp ~ 2^447  true b*_m[m] = 2^-158  dominated: True

